⭐ S3 (Simple Storage Service)
 Amazon S3 stands for "Simple Storage Service". 
 It is an object storage service provided by AWS. 
 We use S3 to store files such as images, videos, documents, backups, and website files. S3 provides high durability, scalability, and security.

📌 Simple Example
Suppose you have a website 🖥️ and users upload profile photos 📸.
Instead of storing photos on your computer or server:
User → Upload Photo → S3 Bucket → Photo Stored ☁️

🔑 Important S3 Terms
Bucket → Container where files are stored.
Object → Actual file like image, video, PDF.
Key → Unique name/path of an object.
Region → AWS location where the bucket is created.
Storage Class → Defines storage cost and access type.

>> key point
Storage Type: Object Storage
Maximum Object Size: 50 TB (actual limit about 48.8 TiB)
Console Upload Maximum: 160 GB
Maximum Bucket Size: No limit
Objects in Bucket: No limit
Durability: 99.999999999% (11 9's)
File in S3: Called Object
Object Storage Place: Called Bucket
Large File Upload: Multipart Upload
Multipart Maximum Parts: 10,000
Security: IAM, Bucket Policy, Encryption

