⭐ EBS (Elastic Block Store) 
“Amazon EBS stands for Elastic Block Store. It is a block storage service provided by AWS. It is mainly used as a storage disk for EC2 instances.”

📌 Simple Example
EC2 = Computer 🖥️
EBS = Hard Disk 💾

>> use case:
EC2 Storage → Used as a hard disk for EC2
Operating System → Store Windows or Linux OS
Application Data → Store application files
Database Storage → Store database data
Backup → Create EBS Snapshots
Extra Storage → Add more storage to EC2


>> key point:
Storage Type: Block Storage
→ Data ko small blocks me store karta hai.

Use: Store OS, Apps, and Data
→ EBS me Operating System, applications aur files/data store kar sakte hain.

Maximum Volume Size: Up to 64 TiB
→ Ek EBS volume ka size volume type ke according 64 TiB tak ho sakta hai.

Location: Availability Zone (AZ)
→ EBS volume ek specific Availability Zone me create hota hai.

Backup: EBS Snapshot
→ EBS data ka backup Snapshot ke through liya jata hai.

Security: Supports Encryption 🔐
→ EBS data ko encryption se secure kar sakte hain.

Size: Can Increase Volume Size
→ Zarurat padne par EBS storage size ko increase kar sakte hain.

Types: gp3, gp2, io1, io2, st1, sc1
→ EBS ke different volume types hain, jo performance aur use-case ke according select hote hain.



