⭐ EFS (Elastic File System)
Amazon EFS is a file storage service used to share files between multiple EC2 instances.

🎤 Simple Interview Answer
“Amazon EFS stands for Elastic File System. It is a file storage service provided by AWS. Multiple EC2 instances can access the same EFS storage at the same time.”

>> Use Cases
Shared File Storage
Multiple EC2 instances access same files
Web applications
Content management systems
Application shared data
Automatic storage scaling

⭐ Glacier
Amazon S3 Glacier is a low-cost storage service used to store data for a long time.

🎤 Simple Interview Answer
“Amazon S3 Glacier is an archive storage service provided by AWS. It is used to store data that is not accessed frequently for long-term backup at a low cost.”

>> Use Cases
Long-term data storage
Data backup
Old files storage
Company records
Financial records
Archive data


